<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Step templates are the building blocks in the toolbox. Admins manage them on
        <a href="/manage/projectiontemplates">Projection Templates</a>. Most venues never need to change them.
    </FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li>Select a template to edit its <strong>Template Name</strong>, <strong>Description</strong> and
            <strong>Parameters</strong>, or start a new one.</li>
        <li>Each parameter has a <strong>Name</strong> and a <strong>Data Type</strong>: String, Integer, Float,
            Boolean, DateTime, File, VideoFile or Dashboard. That decides what kind of box people fill in on the step.</li>
        <li>Save your changes, or delete the selected template.</li>
    </ul>
    <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
        Kiosks only know how to show the built-in templates (Show Text, Play a Video, Dashboard, Live Capture
        and Delay). Don't rename these, or delete their parameters. A new template won't show anything on a kiosk
        until it's supported there.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
